[h1]TLB Keys[/h1]
[b]Vehicle keys for Arma 3 with ACE3, set up the way your unit plays. Lock it for your side, your squad, or one key.[/b]

ACE's vehicle keys open every vehicle of a side, and there is no good way to hand one out in the middle of a mission. TLB Keys replaces them with keys your players manage in the field, from the ACE interaction menu or a key binding.

[h1]Locking a vehicle[/h1]
A vehicle nobody has locked is open. The first player to lock one becomes its owner and chooses who else it opens for:
[list]
[*][b]Every key of the side[/b] - anyone carrying a blank key of the vehicle's side.
[*][b]The owner's squad[/b] - the owner's squad, carrying a blank key of the side.
[*][b]Paired keys only[/b] - only keys cut to that vehicle. The owner's key is cut as it is locked.
[/list]

[h1]Features[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Spare keys[/b] - cut a blank key to the vehicle and hand it to someone.
[*][b]Change locks[/b] - every key cut for the vehicle stops fitting, spares included.
[*][b]Master keys[/b] - one per side, for Zeus, command and the motor pool. Opens and manages every vehicle of that side, however it is locked.
[*][b]Key fobs[/b] - program one to a vehicle: it opens the vehicle and locks it from a distance, with a chirp.
[*][b]Key bindings[/b] - lock or unlock the nearest vehicle your keys open without opening a menu, plus three key slots for chosen keys.
[*][b]Ignition lock[/b] - no key, no engine, even in the driver's seat.
[*][b]Locked cargo[/b] - a locked vehicle's inventory stays shut to anyone whose keys do not fit.
[*][b]Inside handle[/b] - anyone in a seat can lock and unlock, like a real car door.
[*][b]Hand over key[/b] - an ACE action on another player, so nobody swaps inventories.
[*][b]Inspect and label[/b] - see what a key opens, and name it, so a crate of motor pool keys stays readable.
[*][b]Lockpicking[/b] - with TLB Interactions, vehicles are picked on its board; without it, ACE's lockpick. A picked vehicle is hotwired until someone locks it again.
[*][b]Vehicle types[/b] - choose which kinds of vehicle use keys at all: cars, APCs, tanks, helicopters, planes, boats.
[/list]

[h1]For mission makers[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Key Set module[/b] - sync vehicles, crates and units and they share one set of keys: the vehicles are locked to it, the crates hold its keys, the units spawn carrying one.
[*][b]Master Key module[/b] - synced units start with a master key for their side.
[*][b]Eden attributes[/b] - every vehicle can be given keys, a side, a key set, a start lock state and whether its lock can be picked.
[*][b]Zeus modules[/b] - lock or unlock a vehicle, remove its keys, drop a key for it, or give a unit a master key.
[*][b]Scripting[/b] - public functions to assign keys, hand them out and check access.
[/list]

[h1]For servers[/h1]
Around 40 CBA settings, all server-forced, so a unit can allow one way of using keys or all of them: which modes are allowed, who may lock a vehicle first, who may manage it, spare keys, master keys, key fobs, lockpicking, key bindings and which vehicle types use keys at all.

[h1]Requirements[/h1]
[list]
[*]Arma 3 v2.14 or newer
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=450814997]CBA_A3[/url] - required
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=463939057]ACE3[/url] - required
[*]TLB Interactions - optional, for picking vehicle locks on its lockpicking board
[/list]

Load it on the server and on every client. Server key included for signature verification.

[h1]Documentation[/h1]
